<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			26/6/97		  19/6/97	     28/6/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	400-425			450		   350</p>
<p>    Naphtha		75			 75		    75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,700		    1,800		 1,325</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    275		  300-325		   300</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15			 15		     5</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks fell slightly over the past week but activity was quiet with little product moving in or out of storage.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks slipped as outgoing barrels into Switzerland, Germany, Benelux and France offset incoming material.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks fell on outgoing material for bunkering and some straight run fuel moving into Germany for refinery feedstock.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 4984</p>
</text>
